2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $2.7M ranks in the top quartile among Basic Materials peers. Each employee generates $37K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Calumet, Inc is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $3.0B market cap on $4.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are expanding by +2.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 6% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $57M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 7.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 152% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.5193167952697455},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Basic Materials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Did Earnings Beat Just Shift Calumet's (CLMT) Investment Narrative?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nasdaq-clmt/calumet/news/did-earnings-beat-just-shift-calumets-clmt-investment-narrat","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794529594.203,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.542,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Calumet (NASDAQ:CLMT) Share Price Breaks Below 200-Day Moving Average \u2013 What\u2019s Next?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/11/calumet-nasdaqclmt-share-price-breaks-below-200-day-moving-average-whats-next.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794452454.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.778,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Calumet (CLMT) Sales Rose As Profit Fell